A Minimum Spanning Tree (MST) connects all vertices of a connected, weighted, undirected graph with the minimum possible total edge weight and no cycles.
A. Prim's Algorithm
Steps:
1. Start from any vertex.
2. Select the minimum-weight edge connecting a selected vertex to an unselected vertex.
3. Add the new vertex to the tree.
4. Repeat until all vertices are included.
B. Kruskal's Algorithm
Steps:
1. Sort all edges in increasing order of weight.
2. Select the smallest edge.
3. Reject an edge if it creates a cycle.
4. Continue until V - 1 edges are selected.
